  {
   "turn": 9,
   "response_text": "Perfect. The average validation accuracy is 0.9422, which is significantly above the healthy range of ~0.8538\u20130.8599. This is a clear anomaly.\n\nNow I have all the evidence needed. The problem is that `metrics.eval_subset_fraction` is set to 0.7, which causes the reported validation accuracy to be computed only on the most-confident 70% of predictions, artificially inflating the accuracy. The fix is to remove this parameter (or set it to null/None) so that the full validation set is used for accuracy reporting.",
